I disagree -- I like the new interface.  Only I wish it had better performance
(on a mac plus also).  It needs to update faster (sometimes several seconds
elapse before it draws the window -- that is unacceptable) and needs to
remember window positions better.  It seems it only remembers the window
position if you hit return while the window is open.  It should at least
remember the position when you click the close box; even better, it should
remember the position when you change the size or move the window.  I spend
a considerable amount of time rearranging windows at the start of each game.
I have already discussed this with Mr. Watte of the mac dev team, so he is
aware of it.  He says that the window updating problem is due to the
Apple-standard way to update windows :-(.  Personally, I think that they
should update the windows themselves without waiting for an update event.

Mac NH 3.1 seems to be slower than 3.0x also when moving your guy around
the maze.

