I agree;  I find I don't really need the money all that much anyway while
playing.  If you want to cheat though, here's how to do it.

Spoiler:


First install the Macsbug debugger.  Then take note of the status bar, i.e.
how many experience points and gold you have.  Then hit the interrupt switch,
and make sure Macsbug says Nethack is the active appl (if not, type g <CR>,
then try again).  Then type:
   fl a7 200000 xxxx <CR>
   Hit return a bunch of times to get several matches.
where xxxx is the thing you are looking for.  Look for gold, then do it again
with experience points.  The status variables are probably near where 
matches of your searches coincide.  Once you find the match, display a page
of memory around the match (dp addr).  You can then mangle the status vars
to your liking with the sm, sl, sw, etc., commands.  I'm not responsible
if you screw things up :-).

I did this once, but I found it wasn't really necessary in the long run.
Nethack's gradual increases in both ability, XP, and gold are more than
satisfactory to the average player.

